image(), which worked some versions ago but doesn't anymore; my fix
(committed to svn) now only works with useRasterImage FALSE, whereas
image.default can useRaster WITH breaks set.

I fixed it, creating more spaghetti.

Is there anything against the implementation below, which lets image()
do all this? The function is back from 80 (hard to read) to 40 lines,
mainly dealing with r/g/b specified.

It would let sp depend on R 2.13.0
